But as Robin just said, there currently is no process and we aren't
ready yet to institute one. He said that we first must finish
clarifying the precise meanings and edge use cases of the rarest
cmavo, so that we will be able to verify their usage. We must complete
work on the standard before we can know if a text with weird usages is
conforming to the more esoteric areas of the standard.

However, we all now agree that it is within the BPFK's mandate and
purview to put this on their to-do list.

-Matt


